{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "eAkQVMmwFIvK72hvz",
			"description": "Guardian Spear",
			"local_notes": "The signature Custodian sidearm: a master-crafted disruption-field spear with a bolt caster built into the haft below the blade. Field toggle is a free action, as any power weapon.\n\nLore: The guardian spear is the standard wargear of the rank-and-file Custodian Guard across current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background and Chris Wraight's novels (chiefly Watchers of the Throne: The Emperor's Legion), combining a disruption-field blade with an integral bolt weapon so a Custodian never has to choose between melee and ranged threats. Named Custodians are repeatedly shown fighting one-handed with it despite its size.\n\nDesign: Weight: 55 lb loaded, reasoned up from the framework's own Astartes boltgun figure (35-40 lb) for the added mass of a full polearm haft, an integrated blade, and a Custodian-scale gun mechanism on a weapon built for a 2.5-3 m wielder. Min ST: sqrt(10x55) = 23.5, rounded to 23, marked two-handed (†); Custodian ST 40 is 1.7x that minimum, past the standard 1.5x threshold for one-handed use, which is exactly why the fiction shows Custodians one-handing it. Melee: reach 1,2* and Spear skill as a two-handed thrusting polearm (Basic Set convention); parry 0 as a balanced weapon rather than a clumsy one. Mundane baseline thr+3 imp (one step above the human/Astartes Power Lance's braced thr+2 baseline, reflecting a heavier, Custodes-forged spearhead); field on adds the Custodes power-field bonus (+4d, Armor Divisor 10) for thr+4d+3(10) imp. At Custodian ST 40 (thr = 4d+1 per the Basic Set high-ST damage table) this totals 8d+4 (avg 32): by exact dice distribution it penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 7), Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 10) and Auramite (DR 150, eff. 15) essentially always (100%), Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 20) 99.3% of the time, and even Allarus plate (DR 250, eff. 25) 90.9% of the time - comfortably beating an armoured Space Marine in melee \"most of the time\" as the assignment requires, and remaining a real threat to the very heaviest infantry armour in the setting. Bolt caster: fixed boltgun anchor (6dx2(2) pi++ / 2d cr ex follow-up, framework.md). RoF 3 (semi-automatic mechanism, matching the boltgun convention rather than a slower single-shot action). Acc 3 and range 150/600, both below the dedicated Umbra/Godwyn boltgun's Acc 4 and 200/1000, since the barrel is shorter and buried in the spear haft rather than built as a dedicated long gun. Shots 12(3): a smaller integral magazine than a backpack-fed boltgun's 24, reflecting the space the blade mechanism and haft take up. Bulk -6: bulkier than even an Astartes boltgun's already-heavy -4, since the whole weapon is spear-length and carried as a polearm first, a gun second. Rcl 3, unchanged from the standard bolt round's kick regardless of mount. Against Astartes power armour (eff. 50) the bolt caster penetrates 14.5% of hits, identical to a standard boltgun's own figure, as the framework specifies for its bolt casters.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "50000",
			"base_weight": "55 lb",
