		{
			"id": "e4KB6UDDsqTZvD3pn",
			"description": "Sentinel Blade",
			"local_notes": "A one-handed alternative to the guardian spear, pairing the blade with a praesidium shield or a second sentinel blade. Field toggle is a free action.\n\nLore: Carried by Custodian Wardens and other Custodians who favour a one-handed blade over the spear, often alongside a praesidium shield; consistently depicted in current Codex background as no less deadly than the guardian spear, trading reach for a free hand.\n\nDesign: Weight: 20 lb, reasoned as roughly the combined mass of an Astartes bolt pistol (4-4.5 lb) and Astartes chainsword (14 lb) fused into one Custodes-scale hilt, since it packs a full boltgun-anchor mechanism (see below) and a broadsword-length blade into a single one-handed unit. Min ST: sqrt(10x20) = 14.1, adjusted up to 17 for the leverage/balance penalty of a very dense, front-heavy one-handed weapon (the same kind of upward adjustment the framework's Astartes chainsword takes over its own raw sqrt(10x14)=11.8). Melee: reach 1, Broadsword skill, parry 0 (a well-balanced blade despite its bulk). Mundane baseline sw+2 cut - heavier than the human/Astartes Power Sword's sw+1 baseline, for a Custodes-forged blade with more mass behind the edge; field on adds the Custodes +4d(10) to that mundane baseline for sw+4d+2(10) cut. At Custodian ST 40 (sw = 5d-1) this totals 9d+1 (avg 32.5): penetrates carapace, Astartes power armour and Auramite at 100%, Terminator plate 99.1%, and Allarus plate 91.3% (exact dice distribution) - essentially identical performance to the guardian spear's own melee mode, as befits two patterns of the same underlying Custodes power weapon. Bolt caster: the framework is explicit that Custodes bolt casters use the full boltgun anchor (6dx2(2) pi++ / 2d cr ex) even in this one-handed sidearm, not a reduced pistol-scale round - a deliberate lore point that a Custodian's sidearm hits as hard as an Astartes' primary weapon. RoF 3 (semi-auto, as any bolt weapon on this file). Acc 2 and range 120/400 match the human-scale bolt pistol anchor's own figures, since this is fired one-handed despite the full-power round. Shots 10(3): slightly more than a standard bolt pistol's 8, for a larger Custodes-grade magazine. Bulk -3: worse than a plain bolt pistol's -2 for the added blade housing, better than the guardian spear's -6 since it's still a one-handed sidearm, not a polearm. Rcl 3, unchanged bolt-round kick.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
