		{
			"id": "eNLS2yqusmg-dEnzo",
			"description": "Castellan Axe",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle is a free action, as any Custodes power weapon.\n\nLore: An alternative to the guardian spear for Custodian Guard who favour raw cleaving power over reach, usually paired with a heater/ praesidium shield; current Codex background depicts it as slower to bring to bear than a spear but hitting harder per blow.\n\nDesign: Weight: 45 lb, lighter than the guardian spear's 55 lb spearhead- plus-boltgun assembly (which carries a gun mechanism this axe lacks), so it is reasoned from the Astartes chainaxe (15 lb, a Marine-scale two-handed-capable axe) scaled up roughly three-fold for a Custodes- scale two-handed axe-head plus power-field generator. Min ST: sqrt(10x45) = 21.2, rounded up to 22 (marked two-handed, †) for the extra leverage penalty axes traditionally carry over swords of similar weight. Reach 1, Two-Handed Axe/Mace skill, parry -1 (the standard axe defensive penalty). Mundane baseline sw+4 cut, the highest field-off baseline of any melee weapon on this file, reflecting a genuinely heavy axe-head rather than a blade; field on adds the Custodes +4d(10) for sw+4d+4(10) cut. At Custodian ST 40 (sw = 5d-1) this totals 9d+3 (avg 34.5): penetrates carapace, Astartes power armour and Auramite at 100%, Terminator plate 99.8%, and Allarus plate 96.1% (exact dice distribution) - the single hardest-hitting Custodes power weapon in this file, matching its \"hits harder, handles clumsier\" reputation.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "44000",
