		{
			"id": "e91Ev-zSjM9mM4WyH",
			"description": "Misericordia",
			"local_notes": "A Custodian's personal sidearm/backup blade and traditional execution weapon - drawn to finish a fight the spear or axe can't, or to deliver a clean death to a beaten foe. Field toggle is a free action.\n\nLore: Codex background and Custodes iconography both show a small, ornate power dagger worn at a Custodian's side alongside the primary weapon, named for the mercy-blades of real medieval knights (a misericorde delivered a coup de grace through an armoured opponent's joints) - this project reads the name as deliberately evoking that real-world weapon rather than any single cited in-universe passage.\n\nDesign: Weight: 5 lb - small by Custodes standards but still a substantial blade at their scale, following the same logic as the framework's Astartes combat knife (built on the human Shortsword profile rather than a scaled-up knife, since a \"small\" blade in a Custodian's hand still reads as a functional shortsword). Min ST: sqrt(10x5) = 7.1, rounded up to 9 to account for the dense power-field generator built into the hilt of an otherwise light blade. Reach C,1, Shortsword skill, parry 0. Mundane baseline thr+1 imp, matching the Astartes combat knife's own thrust baseline; field on adds the Custodes +4d(10) to that baseline for thr+4d+1(10) imp. At Custodian ST 40 (thr = 4d+1) this totals 8d+2 (avg 30): penetrates carapace, Astartes power armour and Auramite at 99.9-100%, Terminator plate 97.6%, and Allarus plate 82.1% (exact dice distribution) - a shade behind the full-size Custodes power weapons above, appropriate for a backup blade rather than a primary one, but still lethal even against the heaviest infantry plate in a Custodian's hand.",
