		{
			"id": "eSNMgq0qV-9cnuy7j",
			"description": "Pyrithite Spear",
			"local_notes": "A guardian spear pattern that replaces the bolt caster with a pyrithite promethium-analogue projector; used where an area incendiary effect matters more than a single penetrating round.\n\nLore: Codex: Adeptus Custodes background lists the pyrithite spear among the Custodian Guard's ranged wargear options as a spear-mounted fire weapon; this project has not found a page-precise technical description of the pyrithite compound itself beyond \"burns hotter and clings worse than standard promethium,\" which is the detail this build leans on.\n\nDesign: Melee mode is identical in derivation to the Guardian Spear above (same spearhead, same power field): weight is 3 lb heavier (58 lb) for the fuel reservoir replacing the bolt mechanism's ammunition feed, so min ST rises to sqrt(10x58)=24.1, rounded to 24†; all melee figures otherwise match the Guardian Spear exactly for the same reasons. Ranged mode is built one clear step above the Imperium Flame Weapons file's Heavy Flamer (5d burn, 8-yard cone, ST 12) to reflect pyrithite's \"burns hotter\" reputation and Custodes-grade manufacture, at 6d+2 burn: average 23 penetrates flak (DR 30) only 3.6% of the time and mesh (DR 36) never (exact dice distribution): it burns unarmoured and lightly-armoured infantry and is stopped by any real armour, like the flame family generally, and does nothing to rigid plate (0% vs carapace DR 70). Its real threat against armoured targets is the ignition follow-up, which ignores DR. Cone range (6 yards) sits between the Flamer (5) and Heavy Flamer (8), and the fuel reservoir (5 charges) is smaller than the Heavy Flamer's 6 for the reduced space left by the spear haft. RoF 1 and no Acc follow the shared flame-weapon convention (B412); Bulk -6 matches the Guardian Spear's own polearm-length bulk. The DR-ignoring follow-up is 1d+1, matching the Heavy Flamer's follow-up (the follow-up scaling in the Imperium file plateaus at that rate), and keeps the same sealed-armour exemption used throughout that file.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
