		{
			"id": "eKBjy5laoE7j1tCsa",
			"description": "Adrasite Spear",
			"local_notes": "A rarer guardian spear pattern mounting a short-ranged melta-class thermal projector instead of a bolt caster, for boarding actions and anti-armour work.\n\nLore: This project has not located a confident Black Library or current Codex citation for the \"adrasite spear\" specifically (as distinct from the widely-documented pyrithite spear); it is included here as a plausible archeotech Custodes spear pattern, following the same naming convention as Custodes wargear generally. GM-optional and low-confidence: treat it as a re-skinned meltagun (its ranged lines are the meltagun anchor, borrowed on purpose) until a firmer source turns up.\n\nDesign: Melee mode is identical to the Guardian Spear (same weight-driven ST derivation, same power field), at 60 lb / ST 24† for the extra mass of a thermal reservoir and focusing array replacing the bolt mechanism. The ranged mode reuses the framework's own Meltagun anchor outright (8dx6(10) burn short range, 4dx6(3) burn beyond - see framework.md's weapon table) rather than inventing new penetration numbers for an uncertain weapon: \"adrathic\" is read as the same short-ranged, armour-melting principle as a meltagun, simply built into a Custodes-scale spear rather than a rifle, which is why this entry borrows the anchor's exact figures instead of deriving its own. Range (5/20) is shorter than a standalone meltagun's typical use case, reflecting the shorter, spear-integrated nozzle; RoF 1, Acc 1 and Rcl 1 follow the same single-shot, short-ranged beam-weapon convention the framework specifies for melta-class weapons. Checked by exact dice distribution against both tables: at short range the anchor's 8dx6(10) burn (avg 168) penetrates every personal armour and AV10-14 row at 99.99%+, and the DR 1350 glacis of a Leman Russ front or Land Raider (eff. 135) 87% of the time, matching the framework's own claim that a meltagun \"kills AV14 (eff. DR 44) at short range\". Beyond ½D, 4dx6(3) burn (avg 84) is far less certain: it penetrates carapace (eff. 20) 100%, Astartes power armour (eff. 33.3) 99.6%, Auramite (eff. 50) 94.6%, Terminator plate (eff. 66.7) 76.1%, and Allarus plate (eff. 83.3) 55.6%; against vehicles, AV10 (eff. 41) 98.8%, AV11 (eff. 61) 84.1%, AV12 (eff. 83) 55.6%, AV13 (eff. 113) 9.7%, and AV14 (eff. 146) 0% - identical to the framework's own stated meltagun-beyond-½D figures, so this weapon is a near-certain kill up close and only a threat to light and medium vehicles at range, exactly like the rifle-form meltagun it borrows from.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "55000",
			"base_weight": "60 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "woTetDTkc6eC-vGv2",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "imp",
						"st": "thr",
						"base": "4d+3",
						"armor_divisor": 10
					},
					"reach": "1,2*",
					"parry": "0",
					"strength": "24†",
					"usage": "Spearhead, field on",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -5
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Spear"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Polearm"
							},
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Staff"
							},
							"modifier": -2
						}
					]
				},
				{
