		{
			"id": "e0jDnFdJBuo4FA92Z",
			"description": "Interceptor Lance",
			"local_notes": "Carried one-handed by Vertus Praetors riding Dawneagle jetbikes for mounted charges; this entry is the lance only. A Vertus Praetor's jetbike mounts its own separate hull weapons, not covered here.\n\nLore: Codex: Adeptus Custodes background describes the interceptor lance as the signature weapon of jetbike-mounted Vertus Praetors, used in high-speed charges; this project has deliberately not extended the entry to cover jetbike-mounted guns, since it has no confident, specific source for those weapons' own numbers.\n\nDesign: Weight: 50 lb, comparable to the Guardian Spear's 55 lb since it is a similarly-sized power spear, slightly lighter for a design meant to be swung one-handed at speed rather than braced two-handed. Min ST: sqrt(10x50) = 22.4, adjusted up to 24 (no † - it is used one-handed, at the cost of a poorer parry) to reflect the extra difficulty of controlling such a long weapon one-handed while riding. Reach and mounted-charge structure follow the human-scale Power Lance's own three-line pattern (mounted charge / braced dismounted / field-off mounted charge) from Imperium/Weapons/Melee Weapons.eqp, scaled to the Custodes power-field rule: mundane baseline thr+3 imp braced (as the Guardian Spear) with the lance's usual +1 mounted-charge momentum bonus, field on adding +4d(10). Mounted charge, field on: thr+4d+4(10) imp (mundane baseline thr+4, +4d) = 8d+5 at Custodian ST 40 (avg 33), penetrating carapace, Astartes power armour and Auramite at 100%, Terminator plate 99.6%, and Allarus plate 93.9% (exact dice distribution) - the single most reliable Custodes weapon against the very heaviest infantry plate in this file, fitting its role as a dedicated shock-cavalry weapon. Braced (dismounted) drops to the same thr+4d+3(10) imp as the Guardian Spear's own thrust, since the field itself doesn't care whether the wielder is moving.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
