		{
			"id": "ewJ9LiV-xp5sd60tr",
			"description": "Lastrum Bolt Gun (Sagittarum Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "The long-range bolt weapon of the Sagittarum Guard, the ranged wing of the Custodian Guard. Lower-confidence entry: the role is well attested, the exact technical detail is not.\n\nLore: The Sagittarum Guard are the Custodes' ranged specialists, drawn from Custodians who favour the lastrum bolt gun (a Custodes-grade bolt weapon) over the melee-and-caster spear. This project has no page-precise source for the weapon's specifications beyond its role in current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background, and treats it as a GM-optional entry.\n\nDesign: Uses the fixed Custodes boltgun anchor (6dx2(2) pi++, 2d cr ex follow-up), as every Custodes bolt caster on this file. Handling is set from its role as a precision long gun: weight 42 lb (a little above the Astartes boltgun's 35-40 lb for a longer barrel and Custodes-scale receiver), min ST sqrt(10x42) = 20.5, rounded to 21 and two-handed (†). Acc 5 and range 250/1200 are a step above the Godwyn boltgun's Acc 4, 200/1000 for the longer barrel and dedicated sighting. RoF 3 (semi-automatic, as any bolt weapon), shots 24(3), Bulk -6 and Rcl 3 for a full-length rifle. A Sagittarum jetbike's own guns (hurricane bolters, salvo launchers) are deliberately not modelled: no confident source for their numbers.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
