		{
			"id": "eIF1QKkSFe1N44C2Q",
			"description": "Vexilla",
			"local_notes": "Carried two-handed as a standard/banner, not wielded as a weapon; a GM may allow an improvised-weapon strike with the pole at the usual improvised-weapon penalties, with no bonus from this entry.\n\nLore: A Custodian vexillary carries a vexilla - an ornate banner or standard - into battle as a rallying point and a mark of the formation's importance; current Codex background frames this as primarily a morale and ceremonial role rather than a combat one.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a small Leadership skill bonus (+1) and a modest reaction bonus for allies who see it raised, rather than any weapon profile, per its lore role as a standard rather than a wargear item; no framework anchor applies since it deals no damage.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "8000",
			"base_weight": "15 lb",
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "skill_bonus",
					"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
					"name": {
						"compare": "is",
						"qualifier": "Leadership"
					},
					"amount": 1
				},
				{
					"type": "reaction_bonus",
					"situation": "from Imperial forces who see it raised in battle",
					"amount": 2
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eW4Q9Ie-tj6eVf5s-",
			"description": "Praesidium Shield",
			"local_notes": "The physical shield only (Basic Set Large Shield stats, DB 3): most Custodian Guard carry a plain praesidium shield rather than a Storm Shield's added energy field, per current Codex background.\n\nLore: A round or kite-shaped ceremonial-yet-functional shield carried by Custodian Guard alongside a sentinel blade or castellan axe, consistently depicted across Codex: Adeptus Custodes art and background as a plain (if beautifully made) physical shield rather than an energy-shielded item.\n\nDesign: Weight: 25 lb, heavier than the Astartes Boarding Shield (15 lb) for Custodes scale and materials; min ST: sqrt(10x25)=15.8, rounded to 16 - trivial for a Custodian at ST 40, matching the ease with which they're shown carrying one one-handed alongside a blade. Basic Set Large Shield stats (DB 3, +3 Block) as the Astartes Storm Shield's own physical component; bash damage sw+2 cr, one step above that Storm Shield's sw+1 cr for the heavier Custodes-grade plate.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "18000",
			"base_weight": "25 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "w8RoDdCowkxJyH7O3",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "2"
					},
					"reach": "C,1",
					"parry": "0",
					"strength": "16",
					"usage": "Shield bash",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Shield"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "block",
					"amount": 3
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eCL3lC_tNMmpc4Rxg",
			"description": "Storm Shield, Custodes Pattern (Field Component)",
			"local_notes": "Shield 220 SP. Recharge: after 2 seconds without taking damage, regains 25 SP per second. Covers only attacks from the front and the shield-arm side, as the Astartes storm shield. The physical shield's Defense Bonus and bash are the Praesidium Shield entry above; a Custodes storm shield combines that physical shield with this field.\n\nLore: Custodian storm shields use the same front-and-side energy dispersion field as an Astartes Terminator's, per current Codex background, but built to Custodes-grade archeotech standards - background repeatedly shows them shrugging off blows (including heavy weapons fire) that would break an Astartes' own storm shield outright.\n\nDesign: Built on the same regenerating-shield rules as the Astartes Storm Shield (Field Component) in Imperium/Armour/Force Fields.eqp (160 SP, 2s delay, 20 SP/s), scaled up per the framework's instruction that Custodes tech clearly outclasses Astartes equivalents: 220 SP (+37.5%) and a faster 25 SP/s recharge. Checked against a lascannon (8dx8, avg 224): the Astartes storm shield's 160 SP stops it outright only 6.1% of the time (needs a roll of 20 or less on 8d); this Custodes pattern's 220 SP stops it 46.0% of the time (needs 27 or less) - \"clearly outclasses\" in concrete terms, turning an occasional save into a coin-flip, while still not making a Custodian invulnerable to the heaviest weapons in the setting. A plasma bolt (6dx4, avg 84) is stopped outright by either shield essentially always.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "28000",
			"base_weight": "6 lb",
			"uses": 220,
			"max_uses": 220,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "e2XUAGHZQa5kGEmup",
			"description": "Balistus Grenade Launcher",
			"local_notes": "A rotary-fed, multi-role grenade launcher carried and fired one- handed by a Custodian; each shell type is loaded in its own rotary cylinder rather than mixed in one magazine.\n\nLore: Codex: Adeptus Custodes background lists the balistus grenade launcher as squad-level Custodian Guard wargear, firing both anti-personnel and anti-armour shells; treated as a support option rather than every Custodian's default loadout.\n\nDesign: Weight: 30 lb, reasoned as a Custodes-scale support weapon roughly twice the mass of the Astartes Heavy Bolt Pistol family (6 lb) for a full rotary-cylinder launcher, still light enough to fire one-handed at Custodian ST. Min ST: sqrt(10x30)=17.3, adjusted up to 20 for the awkward mass distribution of a rotary-fed launcher versus a slender rifle of similar weight. RoF 1 (single shell per trigger pull, cylinder rotates between shots rather than firing automatically); Shots 6(3) for a six-chamber cylinder with a fast Custodian reload. Bulk -6 (as bulky as a genuine support weapon); Rcl 2 (a braced, high-mass launcher absorbs recoil better than a rifle). Frag shell reuses the standard bolt-family fragmentation bracket logic (6d cr ex [3d cr], no armour divisor, anti-personnel only) rather than inventing a new mechanic. Krak shell is scaled one clear step below the framework's Krak Missile anchor (6dx6(5) cr, full missile-launcher scale) at 6dx4(3) cr (avg 84) for an infantry-portable shaped charge: by exact dice distribution it penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 23.3) 100%, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 99.9%, Auramite (DR 150, eff. 50) 98.0%, Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 85.5%, and Allarus plate (DR 250, eff. 83.3) 54.6% - genuinely dangerous to any infantry target, as a shaped charge should be. Against vehicles it drops off faster than the full Krak Missile anchor: AV10 (DR 125, eff. 41) 99.5%, AV11 (DR 185, eff. 61) 90.4%, AV12 (DR 250, eff. 83) 54.6%, AV13 (DR 340, eff. 113) only 3.6%, and AV14 (DR 440, eff. 146) 0% - a real threat to light vehicles and a coin-flip against medium armour, not a substitute for a dedicated krak missile or lascannon against the heaviest tanks.",
