		{
			"id": "eqBsNVu0bsO4EaMiC",
			"description": "Executioner Greatblade",
			"local_notes": "An ordinary (human-scale) disruption-field weapon; field toggle is a free action.\n\nLore: Sisters of Silence are depicted (Codex: Adeptus Custodes background, which covers the Sisterhood, and The Master of Mankind) wielding large two-handed power blades as their signature weapon; this project has no page-precise technical citation beyond that consistent visual and narrative depiction.\n\nDesign: Weight: 9 lb, following the framework's Relic Blade (8 lb, an Astartes-strength two-handed blade) scaled slightly heavier for a dedicated two-handed executioner's sword rather than a duelling blade. Min ST: sqrt(10x9)=9.5, adjusted up to 12 to keep it a genuine two-handed weapon for an unaugmented (if exceptional) human, in the same range as the Eviscerator (13) and Blessed Blade (10 one-handed) already in the Imperium armoury. Reach 1,2, parry -1, Two-Handed Sword skill. This is the general human power-field rule (+3d, Armor Divisor 10 - not the Custodes-specific +4d, since Sisters of Silence are unaugmented humans, not Custodians) applied to a two-handed greatsword's Basic Set baseline (sw+3 cut, as the Relic Blade's own mundane baseline): field on gives sw+3d+3(10) cut. At the Sister of Silence template's ST 12 (sw = 1d+2) this totals 4d+5 (avg 19): by exact dice distribution it penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 7) 100%, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 10) 99.6%, Auramite (DR 150, eff. 15) 84.1%, Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 20) 33.6%, and Allarus plate (DR 250, eff. 25) 2.7% - a mortal woman's power blade reliably beating even Astartes plate, which matches the framework's general \"the disruption field shears power armour whoever holds it\" instruction and the fiction's own depiction of Sisters of Silence as extremely dangerous melee combatants despite carrying no Astartes- or Custodes-grade augmentation.",
