		{
			"id": "eclATDeZOD-IoaTYz",
			"description": "Psyk-Out Grenade",
			"local_notes": "A small anti-personnel grenade with a secondary anti-psyker/anti-daemon payload.\n\nLore: Psyk-out grenades are Codex-listed Sisters of Silence wargear, described as disrupting psykers and harming daemons on top of their ordinary anti-personnel fragmentation effect; the exact game mechanism behind the anti-warp payload isn't detailed in the sources this project drew on beyond \"hurts psykers and daemons especially.\"\n\nDesign: Fragmentation component built the same way as the bolt family's Metal Storm round (a bracketed frag effect, no armour divisor), scaled down to hand-grenade size (4d cr ex [1d cr]) rather than a rifle round's higher base. The anti-warp payload reuses the same underlying idea as the Pariah Gene's Null Aura/Soul-Static Discharge traits (Imperium/Psykers and the Warp) rather than inventing a new mechanic: a burst of anti-psychic \"static\" that staggers a psyker (an Affliction-style HT roll) and does the toxic-style harm a Pariah's touch does to daemons, at a low (0.2) armour divisor since it's a field effect rather than a physical penetrator - it is not meant to be a primary damage weapon, only the specialist tool this project's Sisters of Silence wargear needs.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Sisters of Silence"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "400",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WccvDHaZ3Oyg6WfJT",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr ex",
						"base": "4d",
						"fragmentation": "1d",
						"fragmentation_type": "cr"
					},
					"accuracy": "0",
					"range": "10/20",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "1(3)",
					"bulk": "-2",
					"strength": "8",
					"usage": "Fragmentation burst",
					"usage_notes": "Thrown weapon; minor conventional anti-personnel effect.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "WBFRkcm0WWcSLsWJ7",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "tox",
						"base": "1d",
						"armor_divisor": 0.2
					},
					"accuracy": "0",
					"range": "10/20",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "1(3)",
					"bulk": "-2",
					"strength": "8",
					"usage": "Warp-suppression pulse",
					"usage_notes": "Affects only psykers, daemons and other warp-touched creatures within the same burst radius as the fragmentation above; treat as an occasional-scope Affliction (HT roll or lose the round's action and suffer the listed toxic damage from psychic backlash) for a psyker, and as ordinary toxic damage for anything daemonic/warp-spawned. Has no effect at all on an unaugmented, non-psychic human or on a Pariah.\n",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -3
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Throwing"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eQlZQ4UCmQXuTwvAj",
			"description": "Witchseeker Flamer (Vratine Pattern)",
			"local_notes": "See Imperium/Weapons/Flame Weapons.eqp's Flamer entry for the full cover and ignition rules this weapon shares.\n\nLore: The Witchseeker flamer (this file also calls it the Vratine pattern) is the Sisters of Silence's standard-issue flame weapon per current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background, used alongside their executioner greatblades for close-quarters purging; no source this project consulted claims the Vratine pattern differs ballistically from a standard Imperial flamer.\n\nDesign: Per the assignment's own instruction, this entry reuses the Imperium Flame Weapons file's standard Flamer values outright (4d burn cone, 5-yard range, 1d burn follow-up, ST 9, Bulk -3) rather than re-deriving new numbers: nothing in the lore suggests the Vratine pattern is ballistically different, only that it is the Sisterhood's own manufacture, so restating the Flamer's own derivation here would just duplicate that file rather than add anything.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Sisters of Silence"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "550",
			"base_weight": "14 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "W8D62Yzdb---bvp74",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn",
						"base": "4d"
					},
					"range": "5",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "4(5)",
					"bulk": "-3",
					"strength": "9",
					"usage": "Cone attack (5 yards)",
					"usage_notes": "Identical mechanics to the standard Flamer entry in Imperium/ Weapons/Flame Weapons.eqp (see that file for the full cover/cone rules); this is a Sisters of Silence-manufactured pattern of the same weapon, not a separate stat line.\n",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Liquid Projector"
							},
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Flamethrower"
							}
						},
						{
